facts:
$(a+b)^2$ is **not** $a^2+b^2$: a square of side $a+b$ also holds two $ab$ rectangles.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (5,5);
\draw (3,0) -- (3,5);
\draw (0,3) -- (5,3);
\draw (0,5) -- (3,5) node[midway, above] {$a$};
\draw (3,5) -- (5,5) node[midway, above] {$b$};
\draw (0,0) -- (0,3) node[midway, left] {$a$};
\draw (0,3) -- (0,5) node[midway, left] {$b$};
\node at (1.5,1.5) {$a^2$};
\node at (4,1.5) {$ab$};
\node at (1.5,4) {$ab$};
\node at (4,4) {$b^2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
